    "image_with_text_html_PkTVyN": {
      "type": "image-with-text-html",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_wBmNzi": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The skin barrier and reactivity",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_EUT67t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The outermost layer of the skin, the stratum corneum, forms an important protective barrier. It helps retain water while limiting exposure to potentially irritating external substances.<sup>3</sup></p>\n<p>In sensitive skin, barrier abnormalities are frequently reported, although barrier impairment is not considered the only cause of sensitivity.<sup>2,3</sup> Neurosensory signalling and inflammatory pathways may also contribute to sensations such as burning, stinging and discomfort.<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>For this reason, an effective skincare approach for sensitive and reactive skin should go <b>beyond simply providing moisture, helping to support the skin barrier, calm discomfort and improve skin resilience.</b></p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_wBmNzi",
        "text_EUT67t"
      ],
